@startuml
!include ../style.puml
title Node files outside the chain databases
entity "Node configuration" as Config <<input>> {
  NodeConf / CasperConf / StorageConf / TlsConf
  network / API / consensus / retention settings
  paths supplied by CLI and configuration
}
entity "TLS certificate and key" as Identity <<files>> {
  certificate : X.509
  private key : configured key file
  public key derives peer identity
}
entity "Genesis inputs" as Genesis <<input>> {
  validator public keys and bond amounts
  initial vault addresses and balances
  embedded contracts and token metadata
}
entity "File I/O provisioning" as Provisioning <<input>> {
  logical root identities
  operator paths and capabilities
  static / dynamic execution modes
}
entity "LMDB environment" as Env <<directory>> {
  data.mdb : database pages
  lock.mdb : LMDB coordination
  named databases share one environment
  map size is not allocated disk usage
}
entity "Bounded log files" as Logs <<output>> {
  tracing events and operational fields
  rotation / byte limits
  not consensus state
}
entity "Detached DAG capture" as Capture <<diagnostic>> {
  SnapshotData / DetachedBlock / Coverage
  bounded forensic capture
  not the filesystem WAL snapshot format
}
entity "known-peers" as Peers <<file>> {
  one PeerNode address per line
  sorted unique addresses
  parsed peer ID, host, and ports
  temporary write, fsync, rename, directory fsync
}
Config --> Identity : configured paths
Config --> Genesis : genesis settings
Config --> Provisioning : provisioned roots
Config --> Env : data directory
Config --> Logs : logging settings
Config --> Peers : data directory
Env --> Capture : bounded read capture
legend bottom
No credential values are included. Paths vary by configuration.
Sources: configuration/model.rs, node_environment.rs, tracing_init/bounded_file.rs, dag/soak_snapshot.rs.
This page distinguishes inputs and diagnostics from durable consensus tables.
endlegend
@enduml
